So it turns out that I'll make this a YAFAP and a YAAP, because
shortly after I ascended my Valkyrie, I was able to get my Monk to
follow suit.

So, we'll start with the Valkyrie, Sansa. It all began in the early
floors of the DoD, where, between levels 2 and 4, chanced upon three
altars. The first two were useless to Sansa, at least in beginning,
but the third was not only lawful, but after two short sacrifices,
Mjollnir was sitting in her pretty fingers. Down, down, down she
traversed, through the Gnomish Mines, fighting valiantly, and chancing
upon a nice suit of dwarvish mithril. While prowling the town, she
entered Izchak's store, and found nothing that might grant a wish, but
a standard oil lamp to help her travel deeper within the mines. She
reached the bottom, claimed her luckstone, and booked it out. She
abstained from altar camping just yet, her sights set clearly on
Grayswandir, and was lucky enough to get a magic lamp off an enemy
running around Minetown. It was blessed and put to use, a Blessed +2
Grayswandir sitting in her fingers shortly afterwards. Onward she
continued, fighting until she reached the Rat King's floor, where she
faced him down with not just a long sword between his claws, but Fire
Brand itself. Scrolls burned, precious holy water boiled, and a
retreat was demanded. After slaying the foul creature, taking what
little he had, and plunging further down, luck began to turn itself on
Sansa.
 A stash was set up, and in it were meager handful of items, but
nothing truly in need of stashing, she proceeded to Sokoban. There,
she obtained her amulet, but both the mines and Soko had left her
BoH'less, and so she decended into the deeper floors. Fate had it out
for here though. A polymorph quickly destroyed her precious dwarvish
mithril, along with a cloak. So she fought as an ogre (I think -.-)
until she once again became herself, but by then, much was in need of
work. Again, fate mocked her. A portal out of nowhere carried her to
Vecna's lair, and not only to his lair, but straight to his chamber.
Short a few valuble pieces of armor, and with Vecna hot on her heels,
she fled. Vecna seemed to laugh as he cornered her, a single spell
cast causing damage beyond belief! (89 points O.o) Down to a mere 15
health, and cornered, she drew her wand of fire and glanced around.
Monsters were constantly appearing from nowhere, some of the most
intimidating beings she had ever faced. Liches, Vampires, Vecna
himself stood in front of her. She engraved the E-Word, and tried to
recuperate. Yet it seemed perhaps not all was lost, as the creatures
of Vecna's creation had pinned him, preventing his fleeing (for there
is no staircase where he might teleport away and recover at) and soon
he was naught but a hand. Claiming the hand and his key (after
recovering her hit points, of course) she set out to finish what had
been created in the dark room. Many had stumbled onto the portal by
accident, flooding the dungeons of doom with liches and the like, but
Sansa trekked on, destroying them one by one.
The journey hadn't left her unscathed however, and by the end, she had
been reduced to armor scrounging, with only a cloak and shield on her
to keep her protected. She felt the telepathic message from Norn, and
scouted out her quest. Her AC was still negative via divine
protection, but fate had darker plans. After discovering her quest
portal and proceeding down a floor, her hit points took another spill
from the giants and ants, and she attempted a prayer. Little did she
know here timer was not ready for her, and away went 6 points of
protection, and her last true defense from the fiends around her. She
fled her quest, and struck the wyrm caves. Dragons fell before her
now, as she had dipped for Excalibur along the way (what else could be
done?) and two-weaponing had commenced. She fought valiantly, and
claimed Shimmering Dragon Scales for her effort. Still, no BoH meant
keeping scrolls anywhere near the possibility of fire, and her stash
had little as it is. She was lucky enough to have a single scroll of
Enchant Armor on her, but alas, it was cursed. She proceeded in
gathering holy water and blessing it, making it stalwart and ready to
face any foe (and conferred displacement is super-useful).
Next up came One-Eyed Sam, the Black Marketeer. She trudged through
his room, scouting for the most vital item that could be in Sam's
store, a wand of teleportation. However, despite already indentifying
it (via a Giant who zaps it whenever she gets close), she had none of
her own, and simply did the major part of the sorting in the store.
She did, however, find a wand of wishing with one charge left inside.
She did what she had to do, first charging scrolls, and then a wand of
teleportation. Unfortunately, she mispelled the first time she wished
for it, and recieved a wand of opening, but with two wishes left on
the wand (one from a zap left, and one to be wrested) she got what she
needed; while many would consider the /ofTeleportation a trashy wish,
it allowed her to claim the larger part of One-Eyed Sam's loot,
including a MR Cloak and some other goodies. Prior to any action in
the store though (yes, its a little out of order, sorry), she had run
into a tool shop a floor above Sam's, and claimed a BoH for her
troubles. With it, she packed off with Sam's loot (including the
Sunsword, which had been generated, just to be spiteful) and fled,
removing Sam with her wand, and forcing the generated soldiers out of
her way via the same method. One soldier remained in front of the
portal, and she disposed of him quickly, as her /ofTeleportation had
zapped its last charge for a while. She proceeded from that place to
retreat up in Dlvl's to find and slay Nightmare (for the Key of Law)
and armor herself with that last few wishes. Speed Boots now
comfortably on her feet, she descended to Medusa's floor. To her
amusement, as she blinded herself, Medusa simply slaid herself by
gazing at the "oR, and so Sansa proceeded to the castle. a

